course: dictionary
lesson: 6562
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Niche is one of them, and the words around it tell you which meaning to use. «She found her niche in drama» is not about a hollow in a wall. Here niche means a job or activity that suits someone perfectly.
explain: In «In science lessons different species avoid competing because they fill different niches», the clue is science. Niches here means the role and place each living thing has in its habitat, such as what it eats and where it lives. A «niche hobby» is different again: it is something only a small group of people enjoy.
explain: Always ask which meaning fits the sentence. Choose a meaning, put it in place of the word, and check that the sentence still makes sense. If it does not, try the next meaning.
fact: A niche is a small hollow or alcove built into a wall, often to hold a statue or ornament.
fact: A niche can also be a job, place or activity that suits someone perfectly.
fact: In science, an ecological niche is the role and place a living thing has in its habitat: what it eats, where it lives and how it survives.
fact: In business talk, niche describes something that only a small group of people like or buy, such as a niche hobby.
fact: «The letters of CHIEN can be rearranged into NICHE, and une niche is a dog's kennel.» Une niche is French, so the same spelling can have a different meaning in another language.
exercise: What does niche mean in «She found her niche in drama»? | A dog's kennel | A small hollow built into a wall | *A job or activity that suits someone perfectly
exercise: In science, what is an ecological niche? | A small hollow in a church wall | A rare hobby that only a few people enjoy | *The role and place a living thing has in its habitat
exercise: What does a niche hobby mean? | *A hobby that only a small group of people enjoy | A hobby that everyone in the country plays | A hobby you do inside a hollow in the wall
test: In «a statue stood in a niche in the wall», what does niche mean? | *A small hollow built into a wall | A job that suits you | A kind of animal | A word for average
test: Which phrase means something that only a small group of people buy? | *a niche market | find your niche | a statue in a niche | ecological niche
exam: Read «In science lessons different species avoid competing because they fill different niches.» What does niches mean here? | Dogs' kennels | *The roles and places living things fill in their habitat | Little hollows built into walls | Lonely hobbies that few people enjoy
